.TH "cmd_free" "3" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server library"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq
#include \(dqcommand.h\(dq

void cmd_free(COMMAND *cmd);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Recursively frees a \f[CR]COMMAND\f[R] tree produced by
\f[CR]cmd_deserialize()\f[R].
Walks the tree and frees all nested structures including:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]COMMAND\f[R] nodes
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]SIMPLE_COM\f[R], \f[CR]CONNECTION\f[R], \f[CR]FOR_COM\f[R],
\f[CR]IF_COM\f[R], \f[CR]WHILE_COM\f[R], \f[CR]CASE_COM\f[R],
\f[CR]GROUP_COM\f[R], \f[CR]SUBSHELL_COM\f[R], \f[CR]FUNCTION_DEF\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WORD_LIST\f[R] chains and their \f[CR]WORD_DESC\f[R] entries
(including \f[CR]word\f[R] strings)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]REDIRECT\f[R] chains (including \f[CR]redirectee.filename\f[R]
words and \f[CR]here_doc_eof\f[R] strings)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]PATTERN_LIST\f[R] chains (including patterns and action commands)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]source_file\f[R] strings in \f[CR]FUNCTION_DEF\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]Do not\f[R] use this function on COMMAND trees produced by the bash
parser (\f[CR]parse_and_execute\f[R]); those use bash\(cqs internal
memory management.
This function is only for trees allocated by
\f[CR]cmd_deserialize()\f[R].
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]cmd\f[R] \(em Pointer to the root COMMAND node to free.
May be NULL, in which case the function returns immediately (no\-op).
.SH RETURN VALUE
None.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]cmd_deserialize\f[R](3), \f[CR]cmd_serialize\f[R](3)
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
This function calls the internal \f[CR]cmd_free_recursive()\f[R] which
dispatches to type\-specific free routines based on
\f[CR]cmd\->type\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
Safe to call with NULL at any level of nesting (all recursive calls
check for NULL before dereferencing).
.IP \(bu 2
Connection commands free both \f[CR]first\f[R] and \f[CR]second\f[R]
children recursively.
